  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Morning Dew** (1 review): Reviewer singles out the Morning Dew into Deal sequence as phenomenal [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Hey Jude**: rare: 13 archived performances [5]\n- **Wang Dang Doodle**: rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n- **William Tell Bridge**: rare: 14 archived performances [5]\n- **Playing in the Band Reprise**: rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2022-07-16.DeadCoCitiFieldQueensNYNAk700s** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 193 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer found the recording far better than the bass-heavy upper-bowl stadium sound, where instruments barely came through except during solos [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The recordings come from the closing shows of the tour at Citi Field in Queens [2]\n- Listener in the stadium's upper bowl says speakers were bass-heavy and production highlighted solos slightly late; the night closed the tour [3]\n- Reviewer treats this show as the end of the summer tour [4]\n- Lineup listed: Bob Weir on guitar and vocals, John Mayer on guitar and vocals, Oteil Burbridge on bass and vocals [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2022-07-16.DeadCoCitiFieldQueensNYNAk700s**: taped by JT/NY; transferred by JT/NY; source: Aud > Nak 700's w CP 701 Caps > GAKable's > Lunatec V3 > Sound Devices 722 @ 24/96 [1]. Also: Edited and tracked in Sound Forge Pro 12.0, then converted to FLAC with Traders Little Helper [1]",
